Patch T5 oracles (rung 1b, task T5): protect eng-net-wire's golden vectors
and its never-panic harness.

- crates/eng-net-wire/tests/layout.rs becomes tests/golden.rs, the wire
  format's golden vectors (PROGRESS.md proposal 9): one message of each
  kind, every byte written out by hand. crates/*/tests/golden.rs is
  protected already, so the rename is what protects them.
- crates/eng-net-wire/tests/never_panic.rs joins protected.toml and
  .github/CODEOWNERS (proposal 8, amendment 11): criterion 11's
  never-panic, canonical-bytes and round-trip properties.
- tests/wire.rs's header names golden.rs.

Base: main with the commit that adds this file (rung 1b, T5). At the repo
root, run `git apply` with this file, then `cargo xtask quick`. Session
17's PROGRESS.md entry says how it was tested.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

